{"title":"2026 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 4b","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a <i>Dunbar sequence</i>,\n</p>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc;\">\n<li>each term is a positive integer,</li>\n<li>the second term is greater than the first term, and</li>\n<li>each term after the second is calculated by adding the two previous terms in the sequence.\n</li></ul>\n<p>For example, the first six terms of the Dunbar sequence with first term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and second term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/c/e3c8bef9ece75fbff2fe0e15ee7b9737dde293cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 5, 7, 12, 19, 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"17\" /></center> \n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that the first and second terms in a Dunbar sequence are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. Determine all possible pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28e24c43456d95b5ab8d4f2f8f85a644e98b7ed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> for which the sixth term of the sequence is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17f1d39d686be9b35cb35cc512559edffbfbfcd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$104$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/2/5c2614954c82bb4cd29d85a44316ce4f2a222bdd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /><sup>th</sup> term of the Dunbar sequence. Repeatedly using the fact that \"each term after the second is calculated by adding the two previous terms in the sequence\" for a Dunbar sequence, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/b/83b075afb99a678ec634a544beaa353ce6e21430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{1} + d_{2} = d_{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/7/22743d523813d6927836693b056383847c266c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{3} = a + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/0/b6056fdfa31b5c69a63420f8a081274fedbc9f2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{2} + d_{3} = d_{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/e/c6e0a6b1f3ed4770d60d2b91f3d8327cdbe2bcb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b + a + b = d_{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/f/0cf7afbf6582b727ed4b15e5e2a55dfffe1c29c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{4} = a + 2b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/f/2cf04f012b6946fcf5c6d3b9442d6fe36d544e77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{3} + d_{4} = d_{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3039749a0f7af7212bf7dabdfbd5611256f239.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + a + 2b = d_{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"154\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/6/416722500ffc1a786e982d39f1c99bb6ea596bc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{5} = 2a + 3b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/f/c7fc6c9d82d812d25035a5b95ae2224266f0748d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{4} + d_{5} = d_{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/1/261a7f932843cdac1e91d98bee2843472293bdf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + 2b + 2a + 3b = 104$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"182\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed52b914334c914f3a9a42837af7135bd4afa1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a + 5b = 104$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"111\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>We can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> must be less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd59dbe0a30012940c1499a675b5dfe082d3aaec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\times 20 = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" /> is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17f1d39d686be9b35cb35cc512559edffbfbfcd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$104$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/5/be55103fcd37de50689c2a182b01c457a88912f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\times 21 = 105$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" /> is more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17f1d39d686be9b35cb35cc512559edffbfbfcd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$104$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> also must be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the first term and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is the second term in a Dunban sequence. \n</p><p>Setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/7/397fd7b1f33bdbf6ee27a83d1bcee42d222cb331.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/4/de4d31fe8dc46699c566a57c330722f00dc6cd9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8b$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> would be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17f1d39d686be9b35cb35cc512559edffbfbfcd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$104$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, we see that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/8/18850c5a6f67139956c8c1e35094c0a864ecb8ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b &gt; a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> to be true, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/1/50155c44ce5f98d9e515b4b463237a46d5359d22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b &gt; \\frac{104}{8} = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"108\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Using <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Modular_arithmetic\" title=\"Modular arithmetic\">modular arithmetic</a>, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d8f47df2201fbf28bdccc24a14b13bb942b740.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a + 5b \\equiv 104 \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"183\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/7/657741ae053960c89acb1a1de4171c96f29aa372.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2b \\equiv 2 \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>From this, we then see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/e/7de565d6d5244eee3e66d63fbf1975aff8d3f117.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"18\" />. Alternatively, we could have also used cases where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> was either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and then tested it.\n</p><p>Combining this, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> but less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. From this, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/7/ac7cf037f5598d43952db661dbd18a6a4fe3854c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/6/446be070015a64a1093c03c493200d37be1c8583.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a + 5 \\times 16 = 104$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"144\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/2/3d23c89f70f32cf8ce102a7d74f91f2b473a03e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a + 80 = 104$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/5/2051bb35db8449d90209dbc37729a7d317726b8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a = 104 - 80 = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"155\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/4/494ee37390980f24dd27db714790810f749c7945.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{24}{3} = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>The solution pair is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/0/0d068383d29440caf0dae38239aed676feeae6cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(8, 16)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"63\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/8/1182425bf60d3e368dd7e32af6aa7d9529dd3d51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/5/3e5372016822a1e2191fff1ea424d964ad244cd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a + 5 \\times 19 = 104$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"144\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/d/60d9653ece40a88b95ad3e5a8adc46c96291364a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a + 95 = 104$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/9/4a96fd46c0242daba24857725cf085c98a469f4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a = 104 - 95 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"146\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/9192db8ec13a95945a934cc40ee804ad11421ce1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{9}{3} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>The solution pair is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/1/031e5ad12f2ec62caaf79bb4b33b1e2feec7b1a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(3, 19)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"63\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018034647\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.087 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 208/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 556/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11272/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.760      1 2026_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4\n100.00%    6.760      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36902:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018034647 and revision id 285662. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}